// Title: WMI Persistence - Script Event Consumer File Write
// Sigma ID: 33f41cdd-35ac-4ba8-814b-c6a4244a1ad4
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Thomas Patzke
// Date: 2018-03-07 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1546.003, persistence
// Description: Detects file writes of WMI script event consumer
// False positives:
//   - Dell Power Manager (C:\Program Files\Dell\PowerManager\DpmPowerPlanSetup.exe)
// References:
//   - https://www.eideon.com/2018-03-02-THL03-WMIBackdoors/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_wmi_persistence_script_event_consumer_write.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "C:\\WINDOWS\\system32\\wbem\\scrcons.exe"
